animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+ </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Csalad</i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, <b><i>Malocusians</i></b> and </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Annunaku</i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> are vampires that are tied to their domain, and their disciplines of Lithopedia, Domus and Tenure are all about mastery over it, which makes them shoe-ins for Tzimisce.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I guess they could be koldun, a variant of tzimice that connect with the earth and uses koldun sorcery.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quortulus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525448-putting-vtr-bloodlines-into-vtm#post1525448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+ </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Osites</i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> look corpselike, their hands look especially dead because blood pools in them, and their discipline is death magic. Cappadocians, without a doubt.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought more about Samedi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quortulus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525448-putting-vtr-bloodlines-into-vtm#post1525448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+ </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Khaibit</i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> are hurt by light even more than normal Mekhet, they\u2019re dedicated to the study of ancient knowledge, and they have Obtenebration. The third trait very strongly implies that they would be Lasombra.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is a faction of Lasombra that acts exactly like this and the name Khaibit must have been inspired by Kiasyd, but I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quortulus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525448-putting-vtr-bloodlines-into-vtm#post1525448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+ </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Dragolescu</i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> are all about ghosts, and their discipline of Essentiaphagia is about screwing with ghosts. So despite their Romanian name, they are actually Giovanni.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The name of this discipline makes me think they are more like Nagaraja than Giovanni.<br /> <br /> Sorry to leave all this out in the open, but I haven't really had contact with VTR bloodlines at this level, so seeing this comparison impressed me a little.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T12:44:38-08:00","id":1525471,"title":"","content":"I've never really looked at it, but the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vampire_Translation_Guide\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire Translation Guide</a> exists to accommodate these kinds of crossovers. So that'd be a resource to use for the mechanical parts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think the question that needs to be asked is what you hope to achieve through the mix, precisely?<br /> <br /> Are we talking about the Bloodline mechanic itself, where a sub-set of a Clan gets an additional power with an additional weakness to make up for it? There's probably room for it, though I was never a huge fan of the way that Bloodlines were frequently something you were inducted to *after* the Embrace, rather than just being treated as an aspect of lineage. I understand it's accommodating the fact that this is a game, I just don't care, never liked it.<br /> <br /> Are we talking about their particular Disciplines and such? In a lot of cases, similar powers already exist in VtM precisely because VtR was the sequel, so while particular rituals or abilities might be worth incorporating in some fashion, it may not be worth the effort to translate stuff over when plenty of suitable alternatives already exist.<br /> <br /> Are we talking about the &quot;fluff&quot; of said groups? That's probably the easiest option; just having the Dragolescu be a Giovanni branch family, for example, is pretty straightforward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}